SEGS = {
"3": (
"Richard Hare left behind at his death a long essay titled “A Philosophical Autobiography”, which was published after his death. Its opening is striking:",
"理查德·黑尔去世时留下了一篇题为《一篇哲学自传》的长文，此文在他去世后出版。其开篇十分引人注目：",
"理查德·黑尔（Richard Hare）去世时留下了一篇题为《一篇哲学自传》的长文，在他身后出版。开篇便十分引人注目：",
),
"4": (
"> I had a strange dream, or half-waking vision, not long ago. I found myself at the top of a mountain in the mist, feeling very pleased with myself, not just for having climbed the mountain, but for having achieved my life’s ambition, to find a way of answering moral questions rationally. But as I was preening myself on this achievement, the mist began to clear, and I saw that I was surrounded on the mountain top by the graves of all those other philosophers, great and small, who had had the same ambition, and thought they had achieved it. And I have come to see, reflecting on my dream, that, ever since, the hard-working philosophical worms have been nibbling away at their systems and showing that the achievement was an illusion. (2002: 269)",
"> 不久前我做了一个奇怪的梦，或说半梦半醒的幻象。我发现自己置身于雾中一座山顶，心中十分得意，不仅因为登上了山，而且因为我实现了毕生的抱负——找到一种理性地回答道德问题的方法。但正当我为这一成就沾沾自喜时，雾气开始消散，我看见山顶上四周尽是那些同样怀抱此抱负、并自以为实现了它的哲学家们的坟墓，无论大小。我回想这个梦，终于明白：从那时起，辛勤的哲学之虫便一直在啃噬他们的体系，表明那成就不过是场幻象。（2002: 269）",
"> 不久前我做了个奇怪的梦，或者说半梦半醒的幻象。我发现自己站在雾中一座山巅，心中颇为自得——不仅因为爬上了山，更因为实现了毕生的抱负：找到一种理性地回答道德问题的方法。可就在我为这一成就沾沾自喜时，雾气渐渐消散，我看见山巅四周尽是先我而来的哲学家们的坟墓——无论大家小家的哲学家，都怀有同样的抱负，也都自以为实现了它。回想这个梦，我终于明白：从那时起，辛勤的哲学之虫便一直在啃噬他们的体系，表明那成就不过是场幻象。（2002: 269）",
),
"5": (
"Yet his imagination could also be less modest: a gaggle of moral philosophers is trapped beneath the earth in a smoke-filled chamber; they talk at cross purposes, and refuse to take the way out into the open air that he alone has discovered. It was his ambition to have united elements from Aristotle, Kant, and Mill in a logically cogent way that solved the fundamental problems of ethics (though leaving unfinished business), and he usually believed himself to have achieved this. For much of his career, his “prescriptivism” formed an important part of the curriculum, certainly in Britain. His disappointment was not to have persuaded others (an occasional “we prescriptivists” was always uncertain of reference), and to have left no disciples; he once told John Lucas that this made his life a failure. Yet he leaves behind generations of pupils grateful for the transmission not of a doctrine but of a discipline; and posterity, while unlikely to ratify the logical validity of his theory, will have reason to admire it for its uniting of apparent opposites, freedom and reason, tradition and rationalism, eclecticism and rigor.",
"然而，他的想象也可以不那么谦逊：一群道德哲学家被困在地下烟雾弥漫的房间里；他们各说各话，拒绝走上他独自发现的那条通往露天处所的路。他的抱负是把亚里士多德、康德与密尔以一种逻辑上融贯的方式结合起来，以解决伦理学的根本问题（尽管留下了未竟之业），而他通常相信自己做到了这一点。在其职业生涯的大部分时间里，他的“规定主义”构成了课程的重要部分，至少在英国是如此。令他失望的是未能说服别人（偶尔的“我们规定主义者”总是不确定所指），也未能留下追随者；他曾告诉约翰·卢卡斯，这使他的人生归于失败。然而，他留下了几代学生，他们感念他传承的不是一种学说，而是一种训练；而后来人虽不太可能认可其理论的逻辑有效性，却仍有理由钦佩它把表面的对立、自由与理性、传统与理性主义、折中主义与严格性结合起来。",
"但他的想象也可以不那么谦逊：一群道德哲学家被困在地下烟雾弥漫的房间里；他们各说各话，拒绝走上他独自发现的那条通往户外的路。他的抱负，是将亚里士多德、康德与密尔的成分以一种逻辑上融贯的方式结合起来，以解决伦理学的根本问题（尽管留下未竟之业）；而他通常自认为做到了。在职业生涯的大部分时间里，他的“规定主义”都是课程的重要组成部分，至少在英国如此。令他失望的是，他没能说服别人（偶尔出现的“我们规定主义者”总是不知所指），也没能留下追随者；他曾对约翰·卢卡斯说，这使他的生命成了失败。然而，他身后留下几代学生，他们感念他传承的不是一种学说，而是一种训练；后人虽未必肯认可其理论的逻辑有效性，却仍有理由钦佩它把看似对立的东西统一起来——自由与理性、传统与理性主义、折中主义与严格。",
),
"7": (
"Richard Mervyn Hare was born at Backwell Down, outside Bristol, on 21 March 1919. He was to be known professionally as R.M. Hare, and personally as Dick Hare. His father, Charles Francis Aubone Hare, was director of a firm, John Hare & Co., making paint and floor-cloth; his mother was Louise Kathleen Simonds, of a brewing and banking family. His parents died while he was still young. He was then cared for chiefly by guardians and relatives on his mother’s side, being sent to school first at Copthorne in Sussex, and then, from 1932 to 1937, as a classical scholar at Rugby. He was awarded a scholarship to Balliol College in 1937, where he read two years of Greats before the outbreak of war.",
"理查德·默尔文·黑尔于 1919 年 3 月 21 日出生于布里斯托尔郊外的巴克韦尔·当。他以 R.M. 黑尔为专业之名，以迪克·黑尔为私人之名。他的父亲查尔斯·弗朗西斯·奥博恩·黑尔是一家制造油漆与铺地布的公司约翰·黑尔公司的经理；他的母亲路易丝·凯瑟琳·西蒙兹出身于一个酿酒与银行业家族。他的父母在他年幼时便去世了。此后他主要由母方的监护人与亲戚照料，先被送到萨塞克斯郡的科普索恩上学，随后从 1932 年到 1937 年在拉格比公学作古典学学者。1937 年他获得巴利奥尔学院奖学金，在那里读了两年古典人文学科（Greats），战争便爆发了。",
"理查德·默尔文·黑尔于 1919 年 3 月 21 日生于布里斯托尔郊外的巴克韦尔·当。他以 R.M. 黑尔为专业之名，私下里则叫迪克·黑尔。他的父亲查尔斯·弗朗西斯·奥博恩·黑尔是约翰·黑尔公司的经理，该公司制造油漆与铺地布；母亲路易丝·凯瑟琳·西蒙兹出自一个酿酒兼银行世家。他的父母在他年幼时便已离世。此后他主要由母方的监护人与亲戚照看，先被送往萨塞克斯郡的科普索恩上学，随后于 1932 至 1937 年在拉格比公学攻读古典学。1937 年他获得巴利奥尔学院奖学金，在那里读了两年古典人文学科（Greats），战争便爆发了。",
),
"8": (
"Despite a largely classical education, Hare’s mind was already turning towards moral philosophy. He ascribed this to two things, the need to define an attitude towards fighting, and a feeling of guilt at living in moderate comfort. He spent much time while still at Rugby working with the unemployed, and finally decided not to be a pacifist, but to join the OTC. When war broke out, he volunteered for service in the Royal Artillery, and circumvented the results of a medical test in order to be permitted active service overseas. He was eventually put on a ship for India in autumn 1940. He had a year training Punjabi soldiers, and enjoying some adventures (twice finding his own way back through the jungle, once after losing his guns to the Japanese). He was finally taken prisoner when Singapore fell in February 1942. He then suffered a long march up the River Kwai to near the Three Pagodas Pass, with a group of officers whose task was to work as coolies building the railway from Siam into Burma. So he knew too well the “violent untiring labours” that Aristotle associates with virtue in an ode to a dead friend that was dear to Hare’s heart. He writes in his autobiography, “I prefer to pass over our sufferings during the eight months we were there” (2002: 283); he rarely mentioned them (except when more fortunate critics of his views rashly imputed to him the exemption from a wider experience of life that can be the privilege of an Oxford fellowship). He was eventually imprisoned with fellow officers in Singapore, whence he was released after exactly three and a half years when the War ended.",
"尽管接受的是大体上古典的教育，黑尔的心思已转向道德哲学。他把这归因于两件事：需要确定对待战争的态度，以及因生活于中等舒适之中而感到的愧疚。在拉格比时他花大量时间与失业者一起工作，最终决定不做和平主义者，而是加入 OTC（军官训练团）。战争爆发后，他志愿参加皇家炮兵服役，并规避了一次体检的结果，以便获准在海外参加现役。他最终于 1940 年秋登上一艘开往印度的船。他花了一年时间训练旁遮普士兵，并经历了一些冒险（两次自己从丛林中寻路返回，其中一次是在他的枪被日本人夺走之后）。1942 年 2 月新加坡陷落时，他最终被俘。随后他随一群军官沿着桂河经历了一次长途行军，到达三塔山口附近，这些军官的任务是作为苦力修建从暹罗通往缅甸的铁路。因此他太了解亚里士多德在一首献给亡友、深得黑尔喜爱的颂歌中所与德性相联系的“顽强不息的劳作”。他在自传中写道：“我宁愿略过我们在那里的八个月所遭受的苦难”（2002: 283）；他很少提及这些（除非当他的观点的某些较为幸运的批评者轻率地把豁免于更广泛的生活经验归咎于他，而这种豁免可以是牛津院士身份的特权）。他最终与军官同僚们一起被囚禁于新加坡，战争结束后恰好三年半被释放。",
"尽管所受大体上是古典教育，黑尔的心思却早已转向道德哲学。他把这归因于两件事：一是需要确定对待战争的态度，二是因生活于中等舒适之中而怀有的愧疚。在拉格比时，他花大量时间与失业者一同劳作，最终决定不做和平主义者，而是加入军官训练团（OTC）。战争爆发后，他志愿参加皇家炮兵，并规避了一次体检结果，以便获准赴海外服役。他于 1940 年秋乘船前往印度。他用一年时间训练旁遮普士兵，还经历了一些冒险（两次从丛林中自行寻路返回，其中一次是在枪被日本人夺去之后）。1942 年 2 月新加坡陷落，他终于被俘。随后他与一群军官沿桂河长途行军，抵达三塔山口附近；这些军官的任务是充当苦力，修建从暹罗通往缅甸的铁路。因此，他太熟悉亚里士多德在一首献给亡友的颂歌中所与德性相联系的“顽强不息的劳作”，那首颂歌深得黑尔喜爱。他在自传中写道：“我宁愿略过我们在那里的八个月所遭受的苦难”（2002: 283）；他很少提及这些——除非当他的观点的某些更幸运的批评者，轻率地把那种可以成为牛津院士身份特权的、豁免于更广泛生活经验的特权归咎于他。最终他与其他军官一同被囚于新加坡，战争结束后恰好三年半获释。",
),
"9": (
"After the war, Hare returned to Balliol to complete the four years of Greats. Even before he sat Finals, he was offered a lectureship at Balliol, which almost immediately became a fellowship. Hare always claimed to have learnt a lot from his pupils, and his early years at Balliol granted him outstanding ones—four of whom, Bernard Williams, David Pears, Richard Wollheim, and John Lucas, were to join him both as professional philosophers, and as Fellows of the British Academy. Lucas narrates how he and his contemporaries would plan a day’s campaigning, with a succession of tutees concerting, through the day, objections to some settled opinion of Hare’s, and replies to his replies—with Williams sent in last to deliver the *coup de grâce* that was never, in the event, fatal. No one who never experienced Hare’s impromptu fielding of objections can really understand the resilience of even his less plausible convictions. And yet, despite some impressions, he was quite capable of admitting the force of fair counter-arguments. He had a faith that apparent disagreements can usually be resolved once confusions are removed (whence the over-sanguine title of his last book, *Sorting Out Ethics*, 1997a). This went with a presumption that objections to his views rested on confusion, one that could lead to a degree of asperity. He recognized that the brusquely economical format of his “Comments” within *Hare and Critics* (which he seriously wanted to be titled, after a pub-name familiar in England, “Hare and Hounds”) might be taken amiss (1988a: 201):",
"战后，黑尔回到巴利奥尔完成四年的古典人文学科。甚至在他参加毕业考试之前，他就获得了巴利奥尔的一个讲师职位，几乎立刻转为研究员。黑尔总是声称从学生那里学到很多，而他在巴利奥尔的早年给了他出类拔萃的学生——其中四位，伯纳德·威廉斯、戴维·皮尔斯、理查德·沃尔海姆与约翰·卢卡斯，后来都与他一样成为专业哲学家，并成为英国学术院院士。卢卡斯叙述了他与同代人如何策划一天的运动式辩论，一长串学生在这一天里共同提出对黑尔某种定见的反对意见，以及对黑尔答复的答复——最后派威廉斯上去给予致命一击，但实际上从未致命。从未经历过黑尔即兴应对反对意见的人，无法真正理解即使是他不太站得住脚的信念的韧性。然而，尽管有某些印象，他相当能够承认公允的反驳意见的力量。他有一种信念：一旦混乱被消除，表面的分歧通常可以解决（他最后一本书《整理伦理学》这个过分乐观的书名即源于此，1997a）。这伴随着一种预设：对他的观点的反对意见基于混乱，而这种预设可能导致一定程度的尖刻。他认识到，他在《黑尔与批评者》中的“评论”（他郑重其事地想要以英国一个熟悉的小酒馆之名命名为“黑尔与猎犬”）那种唐突而简略的形式，可能被误解（1988a: 201）：",
"战后，黑尔回到巴利奥尔，完成四年的古典人文学科。甚至在他参加毕业考试之前，他就已获巴利奥尔的讲师职位，几乎立刻转为研究员。黑尔总说从学生身上学到很多，而他早年在巴利奥尔便遇到出类拔萃的学生——其中四位，伯纳德·威廉斯、戴维·皮尔斯、理查德·沃尔海姆与约翰·卢卡斯，后来都与他一样成为专业哲学家，并同为英国学术院院士。卢卡斯讲述了他们这批人如何策划一天的攻防：一长串学生在这一天里接连提出对黑尔某项定见的反对，以及对黑尔答复的再答复——最后派威廉斯上去给予那致命一击，而实际上从未致命。凡未曾亲历黑尔即兴应对反对意见者，无法真正理解即使是他最站不住脚的信念也有何等韧性。然而，尽管给人某些印象，他相当能承认公允反驳的力量。他怀有一种信念：混乱一旦消除，表面的分歧通常便能解决（他最后一本书《整理伦理学》那过分乐观的书名即源于此，1997a）。与此相伴的是一种预设：对他的观点的反对出于混乱，这预设可能引致几分尖刻。他认识到，自己在《黑尔与批评者》中的“评论”（他郑重其事地要用英国一个耳熟能详的酒馆名“黑尔与猎犬”为之命名）那种唐突而简省的形式，可能被误解（1988a: 201）：",
),
"10": (
"> In case anybody thinks that I have been discourteous to my critics in writing notes instead of essays, I must point out that this is what we commonly do to Plato and Aristotle (as in the Clarendon series of commentaries), taking their arguments one by one and treating them briskly but seriously.",
"> 如果有人认为我以写注释而非论文的方式对批评者不礼貌，我必须指出，这正是我们通常对柏拉图与亚里士多德所做的（如克拉伦登评注系列），逐一处理他们的论证，明快而严肃。",
"> 如果有人认为我用注释而非论文来回应批评者是有失礼貌，那我必须指出，这正是我们通常对柏拉图与亚里士多德所做的方式（如克拉伦登评注系列）——逐条处理他们的论证，明快而郑重。",
),
"11": (
"There could be a complaint that Hare was most interested in his own ideas. John Lucas had from Tom Braun a Balliol rhyme (of which he cites a variant version in Lucas 2002: 31)[^lucas-2002] dating from soon after the publication of *The Language of Morals* (1952):",
"也许有人会抱怨，黑尔最感兴趣的是他自己的思想。约翰·卢卡斯从汤姆·布朗那里得到一首巴利奥尔打油诗（他在 Lucas 2002: 31 中引述了一个变体版本）[^lucas-2002]，作于《道德语言》（1952）出版后不久：",
"或许有人会抱怨，黑尔最感兴趣的正是他自己的思想。约翰·卢卡斯从汤姆·布朗那里得到一首巴利奥尔打油诗（他在 Lucas 2002: 31 中引用了一个变体版本）[^lucas-2002]，此诗作于《道德语言》（1952）出版后不久：",
),
"12": (
"> My pupils I have always taught You cannot get an “is” from “ought”. This is the burden of my song: “It’s in my book, or else it’s wrong.”",
"> 我一直教导我的学生 你无法从“是”得出“应当”。这是我歌的副歌： “它在我的书里，否则就是错的。”",
"> 我始终教我的学生： 你无法从“是”推出“应当”。 这便是我歌的旨归： “书里写着，否则即错。”",
),
"13": (
"It is true that Hare was most appreciative of points helpful to his own reconsiderations; he could then be depended upon to be over-generous. He always disparaged his own scholarship, though from a demanding point of view. (Few writers of long books on Plato can have first re-read the whole of Plato in Greek, as Hare did before writing his very short one, 1982.) Yet his interests were wider in range than his publications, and extended through Frege, Chomsky, Davidson, and a fair range of contemporary philosophy of mind and language. Though he was keen to claim ancestry (in a late encyclopedia article he counts Socrates and Aristotle as, in part, the first prescriptivists; 1998: 20), his love of philosophy did not reduce at all to a love of his own philosophy.",
"诚然，黑尔最欣赏那些有助于他自己重新思考的观点；那时可以指望他过分慷慨。他总是贬低自己的学术，尽管是从一个严格的标准来看。（写关于柏拉图的鸿篇巨著的作者中，很少有人能像黑尔那样，在写他那本极短小的书之前，先通读希腊文的柏拉图全集，1982。）然而，他的兴趣范围比他的出版物更广，延伸至弗雷格、乔姆斯基、戴维森，以及相当范围的当代心灵哲学与语言哲学。尽管他热衷于声称谱系（在后期一篇百科词条中，他把苏格拉底与亚里士多德算作——部分地——最初的规定主义者；1998: 20），他对哲学的爱并不完全归结为对他自己哲学的爱。",
"的确，黑尔最欣赏那些有助于他自己重新思考的观点；那时可指望他格外慷慨。他总是贬低自己的学问，尽管是站在严格的标准上。（写柏拉图巨著的作者中，很少有人能像黑尔这样，在动笔写他那本极薄的《柏拉图》（1982）之前，先把希腊文的柏拉图全集重读一遍。）然而他的兴趣比他的著述更广，延伸到弗雷格、乔姆斯基、戴维森，以及相当一部分当代心灵哲学与语言哲学。尽管他热衷声称自己谱系悠远（在后期一篇百科词条中，他把苏格拉底与亚里士多德算作——至少部分地——最初的规定主义者；1998: 20），他对哲学的爱绝不等于对自己哲学的爱。",
),
"14": (
"His most amiable aspects were apparent to the undergraduates (by preference) whom, from early on, he invited to one of his reading-parties, first at Plas Rhoscolyn in Anglesey, and later also at Saffron House in Ewelme, beneath the Chilterns. It was there above all that he vividly communicated a sense of how worthwhile and enjoyable it is not just to read but to *do* philosophy. He was thus, however exacting his standards, a most positive figure as a mentor, giving of himself in discussion in a manner that could be opinionated but was also self-forgetful. He was a Puritan of the traditional kind who shared Dr Johnson’s approval of “harmless pleasures”. He was concerned about the case against eating meat; but his eventual virtual vegetarianism was rather caused, he said, by gardening than by argument. Some of his dislikes were distinctive: the music of Beethoven (which he came to find superficial), wearing socks (which he ascribed to commercialism), drinking coffee (which he said affected his temper), travelling by train (which caused him anxiety), giving and receiving presents (when the recipient best knows what he wants). Ved Mehta (1962) recalls his working, for freedom from interruption, in a caravan on the front lawn of his house in Oxford. He had the courage, though not the extravagance, to be an eccentric.",
"他最令人喜爱的方面，在他（按偏好）邀请来参加他的读书会的本科生面前展现出来，先是在安格尔西岛的普拉斯·罗斯科林，后来也在奇尔特恩山下的埃韦尔姆的萨弗恩宅邸。正是在那里，他生动地传达出一种感觉：哲学不仅是去读，更是去“做”，而这既值得又有趣。因此，无论他的标准多么严格，他作为导师都是一个极为积极的人物，在讨论中投入自己，方式可能固执己见，却也忘我。他是一位传统意义上的清教徒，赞同约翰逊博士对“无害的快乐”的赞许。他关心反对吃肉的理由；但他最终近乎素食，与其说出自论证，不如说出自园艺。他的一些厌恶很独特：贝多芬的音乐（他渐觉浅薄）、穿袜子（他归因于商业主义）、喝咖啡（他说影响了脾气）、乘火车（使他焦虑）、送与收礼物（当收礼者最清楚自己需要什么时）。维德·梅塔（1962）回忆他在牛津宅邸前草坪上的一辆拖车里工作，以求免于打扰。他有勇气——虽无奢侈——做一个古怪的人。",
"他最令人喜爱的方面，在他（按偏好）邀请来参加读书会的本科生面前展露无遗——先是在安格尔西岛的普拉斯·罗斯科林，后来也在奇尔特恩山下的埃韦尔姆萨弗恩宅邸。正是在那里，他生动地传达出一种感受：哲学不仅值得去读，更值得去“做”，而且乐在其中。因此，无论他的标准多么严格，作为导师他都是一个极积极的人物，在讨论中投入自己，方式虽可能固执己见，却也忘我。他是传统意义上的清教徒，赞同约翰逊博士对“无害的快乐”的嘉许。他关心反对食肉的理由；但他最终近乎素食，与其说出自论证，不如说出自园艺。他有些厌恶很独特：贝多芬的音乐（他渐觉其浅薄）、穿袜子（他归因于商业主义）、喝咖啡（他说影响脾气）、乘火车（使他焦虑）、送收礼物（当收礼人最清楚自己要什么时）。维德·梅塔（1962）回忆他在牛津宅邸前草坪的一辆拖车里工作，以求免于打扰。他有勇气做个古怪的人——虽无那样的排场。",
),
"15": (
"It was initially at reading parties that his pupils encountered a part of his life equally important to him as philosophy, his wife and children. What he describes as “a night of mostly bad dreams”, starting with his mother’s death in 1935, ended with his marriage in 1947 to Catherine Verney, which he calls “the best thing I ever did, and a source of lasting happiness” (2002: 272 & 292). They shared a love of traditional Anglicanism (though her beliefs were more orthodox than his), and of music (especially choral and *a cappella*). A Hare reading party at Ewelme was always in part a music camp, with (for all those able to join in) a piano to play and madrigals to sing. Everything equally involved their four children, John (who has published about his father, 2007: 184–248), and three daughters. Without them, he would have felt incomplete even as a moral philosopher; for Aristotle’s question “What sort of person should I be?” gave way, for him, to the question “What sort of person should I bring up my children to be?”",
"最初是在读书会上，他的学生接触到他生活中与哲学同样重要的一个部分：他的妻子与孩子。他所描述为“一个多噩梦的夜晚”，始于 1935 年他母亲的去世，终于 1947 年他与凯瑟琳·弗尼的婚姻，他称之为“我做过的最好的事，以及持久幸福的源泉”（2002: 272 & 292）。他们共同喜爱传统的英国国教（尽管她的信仰比他的更正统），也喜爱音乐（尤其是合唱与无伴奏合唱）。埃韦尔姆的一次黑尔读书会总有一部分是音乐营，有（凡能参与的人）钢琴可弹、牧歌可唱。一切都同样涉及他们的四个孩子：约翰（他写过关于父亲的文章，2007: 184–248）与三个女儿。没有他们，他即使作为道德哲学家也会感到不完整；因为亚里士多德的问题“我应当成为什么样的人？”在他这里让位于问题“我应当把孩子养育成什么样的人？”",
"最初是在读书会上，他的学生才接触到他的一个与哲学同样重要的生活部分——妻子与孩子。他称之为“一个多噩梦的夜晚”，始于 1935 年母亲去世，终于 1947 年与凯瑟琳·弗尼的婚姻；他称这桩婚姻“是我做过的最好的事，也是持久幸福的源泉”（2002: 272 & 292）。他们共同喜爱传统的英国国教（尽管她的信仰比他的更正统），也喜爱音乐（尤其是合唱与无伴奏合唱）。埃韦尔姆的一次黑尔读书会总有一部分像是音乐营：凡能参加者都有钢琴可弹、牧歌可唱。一切都同样牵涉他们的四个孩子：约翰（他写过关于父亲的文章，2007: 184–248）与三个女儿。没有他们，他即使作为道德哲学家也会感到不完整；因为亚里士多德的问题“我应当成为什么样的人？”在他这里，让位于另一问题“我应当把孩子养育成什么样的人？”",
),
"16": (
"Hare remained a tutor at Balliol for twenty years, and always felt attached to that institution above all others (whence the bequest of his *Nachlass*). It was still during his time there, in 1964, that he was elected a Fellow of the British Academy. However, ineluctable promotion eventually removed him, in 1966, to the White’s Chair of Moral Philosophy at Corpus Christi. There he took on a responsibility for the supervision of research students. (Balliol and Corpus Greats pupils still had the benefit of his reading parties, which for a time, while John was at Balliol, became biennial.) He also took his turn as chairman of the Philosophy Panel, which admits and oversees graduates, and chairman of the Faculty Board. Administration, it may be said, was a task with which he coped admirably, but, also admirably, refused to identify.",
"黑尔在巴利奥尔担任导师二十年，始终对那个机构怀有超乎一切的依恋（他的遗稿《Nachlass》的遗赠即源于此）。仍在他任职期间，1964 年，他当选为英国学术院院士。然而，不可避免的晋升最终于 1966 年把他调往基督圣体学院的怀特道德哲学讲席。在那里他承担了指导研究生的责任。（巴利奥尔与基督圣体的古典人文学科学生仍受益于他的读书会，有一阵子，当约翰在巴利奥尔时，读书会改为两年一次。）他还轮流担任哲学委员会主席，该委员会负责招收与监督研究生，并担任学部委员会主席。可以说，行政管理是一项他应付得极为出色的任务，但他也——同样出色地——拒绝认同于它。",
"黑尔在巴利奥尔担任导师二十年，始终对那个学院怀有超乎一切的爱恋（他的遗稿《Nachlass》之遗赠即源于此）。仍在他任职期间，1964 年他当选为英国学术院院士。然而，不可避免的晋升最终于 1966 年把他调往基督圣体学院的怀特道德哲学讲席。他在那里承担起指导研究生的责任。（巴利奥尔与基督圣体的古典人文学科学生仍受益于他的读书会，有一阵子，当约翰在巴利奥尔时，读书会改为两年一次。）他还轮流担任哲学委员会主席——该委员会负责招收与监督研究生——以及学部委员会主席。可以说，行政管理是他应付得极为出色的一项任务，但他也同样出色地拒绝认同于它。",
),
"17": (
"He recalls that most of his cousins on his mother’s side were Americans; and two of his children emigrated to America and married Americans. Like all distinguished Oxford philosophers, he received many invitations there (of which the most welcome was to the Center for Advanced Study in the Behavioral Sciences at Stanford, where he wrote both *Moral Thinking,* 1981, and his little book *Plato*, 1982). All this made less improbable his early retirement from Oxford in 1983, and his appointment as Graduate Research Professor of Philosophy at the University of Florida at Gainesville. One desire was to escape from faculty politics at Oxford. A contributing factor was the publication of *Moral Thinking*, which left him immediately, he confessed, nothing new to say in his staple lectures. Yet his main motive was the prospect of helping to set up a Center for Applied Philosophy.",
"他回忆说，他母方的大多数表亲是美国人；他的两个孩子移居美国并与美国人结婚。像所有杰出的牛津哲学家一样，他在那里收到许多邀请（其中最受欢迎的是斯坦福大学行为科学高级研究中心，他在那里写了《道德思维》，1981，以及他的小书《柏拉图》，1982）。这一切使他在 1983 年提前从牛津退休、并获任佛罗里达大学盖恩斯维尔分校哲学研究生研究教授之职，显得不那么不可能。一个愿望是逃避牛津的院系政治。一个促成因素是《道德思维》的出版，他坦言，这使他在惯常的讲授课上立刻无话可说。然而他的主要动机是参与建立一所应用哲学研究中心的前景。",
"他回忆说，他母方的大多数表亲是美国人；他的两个孩子移居美国，并与美国人结婚。像所有杰出的牛津哲学家一样，他在那里收到许多邀请（其中最受欢迎的是斯坦福大学行为科学高级研究中心，他在那里撰写了《道德思维》（1981）和他的小书《柏拉图》（1982））。这一切使他在 1983 年提前从牛津退休、并出任佛罗里达大学盖恩斯维尔分校哲学研究生研究教授，显得不那么不可思议。他的一个愿望是摆脱牛津的院系政治。一个促成因素是《道德思维》的出版——他坦言，这使他在惯常的讲授课上立刻无话可说。然而，他的主要动机，是参与建立一所应用哲学研究中心的前景。",
),
"18": (
"The very phrase “applied ethics”, now so familiar (and yet, one may think, tendentious), presupposes a tradition of ethical theories, such as his, that invite practical applications. In fact, he published his first paper in practical ethics, titled “Ethics and Politics”, in the *Listener* (1955). (Part of it is collected, under the title “Can I be Blamed for Obeying Orders?”, in Hare 1972a; there it is followed by three papers originally published in the 1950s, and more from the 1960s.) Better known is the last chapter of *Freedom and Reason* (1963), which addressed the issue, then (it seemed) wholly recalcitrant, of apartheid. And much else followed, with a stream of papers, and memberships of various advisory bodies (Hare 2002: 294–5)[^hare-2002]. He was engaged especially by urban planning, where he favored radial over ring roads, and biomedical ethics, in which he labored to be logical and not just *bien pensant*. When a Society for Applied Philosophy was formed, he became its first President. So he looked forward to a profitable refocusing of his energies; and this, to an extent, occurred, even when the Center partly disappointed. As he notes, three out of four volumes of essays published between 1989 and 1993 fall within practical ethics (Hare 1989b, 1992a, 1993a).",
"“应用伦理学”这个短语，如今如此耳熟（然而，人们可能认为，带有倾向性），预设了像他那样邀请实际应用的伦理理论传统。事实上，他在《听众》周刊（1955）发表了他第一篇实践伦理学论文，题为《伦理学与政治》。（它的一部分以《我能因服从命令而受责备吗？》为题收录于 Hare 1972a；在那里它后面是三篇最初发表于 1950 年代的论文，以及更多来自 1960 年代的。）更为人知的是《自由与理性》（1963）的最后一章，它处理了当时（似乎）完全顽固的种族隔离问题。此后还有许多，有一连串论文，以及各种咨询机构的成员资格（Hare 2002: 294–5）[^hare-2002]。他尤其投入城市规划，在其中他偏好放射状道路甚于环状道路，以及生物医学伦理学，在其中他努力做到合乎逻辑而不只是“好心”而已。当应用哲学学会成立时，他成为首任主席。于是他期待一次有益的能量重新聚焦；而这一点在一定程度上发生了，即使该中心部分地令人失望。如他所指出，1989 至 1993 年间出版的四卷论文集中有三卷属于实践伦理学（Hare 1989b, 1992a, 1993a）。",
"“应用伦理学”这个如今耳熟能详（然而人们或许觉得它带倾向性）的说法，预设了一个像他那样召唤实际应用的伦理理论传统。事实上，他最早的一篇实践伦理学论文《伦理学与政治》发表于《听众》周刊（1955）。（其一部分以《我能因服从命令而受责备吗？》为题收入 Hare 1972a；其后是三篇最初发表于 1950 年代的论文，以及更多来自 1960 年代的。）更为人熟知的是《自由与理性》（1963）的最后一章，它处理了当时（似乎）完全顽固的种族隔离问题。此后还有许多：一连串论文，以及各种咨询机构的成员资格（Hare 2002: 294–5）[^hare-2002]。他尤其投入城市规划——在其中他偏好放射状道路甚于环状道路——以及生物医学伦理学，在其中他努力做到合乎逻辑，而不只是“好心”（*bien pensant*）。当应用哲学学会成立时，他出任首任主席。于是他期待一次有益的能量重聚；而这一点在一定程度上发生了，即使该中心部分地令人失望。如他所指出，1989 至 1993 年间出版的四卷论文集中有三卷属于实践伦理学（Hare 1989b, 1992a, 1993a）。",
),
"19": (
"His time in Gainesville was disturbed by the first, and slightest, of his strokes. When he fully returned with Catherine to Ewelme in 1994, further attacks cheated him of his hopes of continuing to combat “the usual misunderstandings” (2002: 304–5). He gave his last paper, appropriately, to an undergraduate audience at King’s College London. He was still able to put together *Sorting Out Ethics* (1997a), deriving from the Axel Hägerström Lectures that he had given at Uppsala University in 1991 (when he also received an honorary doctorate—his first doctorate—from the University of Lund). His eightieth birthday was marked by the publication of a final collection of papers, *Objective Prescriptions and other essays* (1999). He died suddenly but peacefully on 29 January 2002.",
"他在盖恩斯维尔的时光被他的第一次、也是最轻微的一次中风所打扰。1994 年他与凯瑟琳完全回到埃韦尔姆后，进一步的中风发作夺走了他继续对抗“通常的误解”的希望（2002: 304–5）。他最后一次演讲，恰当地，是面对伦敦国王学院的本科生听众。他仍能编成《整理伦理学》（1997a），它源于 1991 年他在乌普萨拉大学所作的阿克塞尔·黑格斯特伦讲座（当时他也获得了隆德大学的荣誉博士学位——他的第一个博士学位）。他的八十寿辰以一部最后的论文集《客观规定与其他论文》（1999）的出版为标志。他于 2002 年 1 月 29 日突然但安详地去世。",
"他在盖恩斯维尔的岁月被他的第一次、也是最轻微的一次中风打断。1994 年他与凯瑟琳完全回到埃韦尔姆后，进一步的中风夺走了他继续对抗“通常的误解”的希望（2002: 304–5）。他的最后一次演讲，恰当地，是面向伦敦国王学院的本科生。他仍能编成《整理伦理学》（1997a），它源于 1991 年他在乌普萨拉大学所作的黑格斯特伦讲座（当时他也获得了隆德大学的荣誉博士学位——他的第一个博士学位）。他的八十寿辰以最后一部论文集《客观规定与其他论文》（1999）的出版为标志。他于 2002 年 1 月 29 日突然而安详地去世。",
),
}
